        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(synology-chat): bound outbound NAS response bodies to prevent Gateway OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Synology Chat outbound calls would unbounded-buffer the NAS HTTP response body into Gateway memory when the chatbot webhook or `user_list` endpoint streamed a large or stuck reply.\n\nInbound Synology webhooks were already capped (`readRequestBodyWithLimit`, #25831). Outbound `doPost` / `fetchChatUsers` still used `data += chunk` with no byte limit (and `doPost` discarded the body after only checking status).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReuse `readRequestBodyWithLimit` from the plugin SDK on both outbound paths:\n\n- chatbot POST responses: **64 KiB** discard budget (status-only)\n- `user_list` GET responses: **1 MiB** parse budget (legacy name → user_id)\n\nOversized chatbot responses fail closed without burning the send retry budget. Oversized `user_list` responses warn and fall back to cache, matching existing error semantics.\n\nProof script stays local (`.local/`, gitignored) so the PR stays small (2 files).\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators running Synology Chat are protected from Gateway memory blow-ups when a NAS (or mis-pointed `incomingUrl`) returns an oversized outbound response. Normal small webhook / user-list replies are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Scope:** 2 files, +154 / -41\n\n**Unit tests:**\n\n```text\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  24 passed (24)\n```\n\nIncludes regression coverage for:\n\n- chatbot response over 64 KiB → `sendMessage` returns false, **1 attempt** (no retry burn)\n- `user_list` over 1 MiB → empty fallback + `exceeded` warn\n\n**Loopback before/after proof** (real `127.0.0.1` HTTP streamer; not committed):\n\n```text\n[proof] BEFORE (unbounded POST drain)\n  would-stream≈25165824 bytes\n  client buffered≈25165824 bytes\n  server wrote≈25165824 bytes\n  ok: negative control absorbed nearly the full stream\n[proof] AFTER (sendMessage + bounded drain)\n  cap=65536 bytes\n  would-stream≈25165824 bytes\n  ok: oversized rejected (sendMessage=false)\n  ok: server wrote≈589824 bytes << would-stream\n[proof] BEFORE (unbounded user_list GET)\n  client buffered≈25165824 bytes\n  server wrote≈25165824 bytes\n  ok: negative control absorbed nearly the full stream\n[proof] AFTER (fetchChatUsers + bounded drain)\n  cap=1048576 bytes\n  would-stream≈25165824 bytes\n  ok: oversized rejected (users=[])\n  ok: server wrote≈1703936 bytes << would-stream\n  warn: fetchChatUsers: response exceeded 1048576 bytes, using cached data\n[proof] small POST response: ok=true\n[proof] small user_list response: parsed 1 user\n\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS PASSED\n```\n\nHead: `662747c67fc91395eb8f6e979422f874deb870a8`\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
